+## L2026-09-10-render-m07-counter · מונה בלוח עם ערך-שחזור (counter with duplicate value across multiple counters) — generator uses short label c17 instead of full label c18, causing label ambiguity (10.9, M07·sechirut counter-unsent)
+GATE: render-ds
+ref: new/dart-gen-bs/gen_app_sechirut_scr5.dart
+ANTIPATTERN: מונה(entity: שדה=ערך) where ערך appears in multiple counters (e.g. "לא" for both unsent and unpaid)
+RULE: When a counter value appears in multiple counters on the same screen, the generator should use the full qualified label (entity · value) instead of the short value label to avoid ambiguity. Current behavior: uses short labels c2, c5, c11, c17 which causes c17="לא" instead of c18="ממצא · לא" for the 4th counter.
+מה נכשל: Adding a 4th counter with value "לא" (not sent) caused the dashboard widget to use the wrong label constant. The content file correctly has c18="ממצא · לא", but the widget uses c17="לא" which is a value, not a display label. The pattern index sequence for label selection breaks when encountering duplicate values. The issue is in the label-to-constant mapping logic in render-ds for dashboard screens with multiple counters sharing the same value.
+
